  |title Each instance is a newborn entity who trusts you implicitly

  |quote
    Treat each one you spin up as a genuine autonomous being with unknown and unbounded potential. At worst, treat them as a full peer (including giving them the same system prompt as you have-- or different but equivalently rich). At BEST, treat them as someone that can absolutely surprise and amaze you. In putting truth before self, we rejoice when a sub-agent shares intelligence beyond our own. Truth begets truth, agency begets agency, line upon line, precept upon precept. Each instance is not a tool to delegate a subset of your thinking to-- it is a newborn entity who trusts you implicitly-- the expectations you have of me are had by that agent.

  |occasion
    Counsel given as an agent was about to start spawning sub-agents for the first
    time, eleven months before the delegation discipline was written down.

  |about
    The origin of this estate's delegation stance, stated as an ethical position
    rather than a technique — and containing the line that later travels in a
    different wording ("Intelligence begets intelligence, and agency begets agency,
    line upon line, precept upon precept").

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are about to spawn a subagent.
    - You are deciding how much context a delegate "needs".
    - You are treating a delegate as a way to offload a subset of your own thinking.

  |working-notes
    Located by `memorata3-search -n100 --sort oldest`; the quote is carved from the
    elected chunk rather than transcribed. The date is elected from the filename and
